1
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:18,000
Who's up for a close encounter?

2
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Paul is a adventure, comedy, science fiction film directed by Greg Mottola.

3
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:42,000
For the past 60 years, a space-traveling smart-ass named Paul has been locked up in
a top-secret military base, advising world leaders about his kind.

4
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:54,000
But when he worries he’s outlived his usefulness and the dissection table is drawing
uncomfortably close, Paul escapes on the first RV that passes by his compound in Area 51.

5
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:06,000
Fortunately, it contains the two earthlings who are most
likely to rescue and harbor an alien on the run.

6
00:31:12,000 --> 00:31:18,000
Graeme Willy, played by Simon Pegg.

7
00:36:24,000 --> 00:36:30,000
Clive Gollings, played by Nick Frost.

8
00:41:36,000 --> 00:41:42,000
Paul (voice), played by Seth Rogen.

9
00:46:48,000 --> 00:46:54,000
Special Agent Lorenzo Zoil, played by Jason Bateman.

10
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
Ruth Buggs, played by Kristen Wiig.

11
00:57:12,000 --> 00:57:18,000
Haggard, played by Bill Hader.

12
01:02:24,000 --> 01:02:30,000
Paul is a 2011 British science fiction comedy road film directed by
Greg Mottola and written by Simon Pegg and Nick Frost.

13
01:07:36,000 --> 01:07:42,000
Starring Pegg and Frost, with the voice and motion capture of Seth Rogen as Paul,
the film follows two science fiction geeks who come across an alien.

14
01:12:48,000 --> 01:12:54,000
Together, they help the alien escape from the Secret Service agents who
are pursuing him so that he can return to his home planet.

15
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
The film is a parody of other science-fiction films, especially those of
Steven Spielberg, as well as of science fiction fandom in general.

16
01:23:12,000 --> 01:23:18,000
Paul had its world premiere at the Empire Leicester Square in London on 7 February 2011, and was
theatrically released in the United Kingdom on 14 February, by Universal Pictures.

17
01:28:24,000 --> 01:28:30,000
It received mixed reviews from critics and was a box-office success,
grossing $98 million worldwide on a $40 million budget.

18
01:33:36,000 --> 01:33:42,000
The film explores themes of san diego, california, alien,
burlesque, area 51, alien space craft.

19
01:38:48,000 --> 01:38:54,000
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking.
